.SH ENVIRONMENT
Environment values are read when the relevant context, transport,
benchmark, or test is created.
.SS "Library and transparent provider"
.TP
.B UIB_PROTOCOL
Select the wire protocol used by newly opened contexts.
.br
Default: rocev2
.br
Accepted values: rocev2, uet, or dummy
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet ./examples/direct_traffic uet\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BIND_IP
Select the local IPv4 address used by the verbs provider.
.br
Default: 0.0.0.0
.br
Accepted values: An IPv4 address assigned to the local host.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BIND_IP=192.0.2.2 LD_PRELOAD=$PWD/libuibv.so app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BIND_PORT
Override the protocol's local UDP or TCP service port.
.br
Default: 4791 for RoCEv2 and 5432 for UET.
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 65535
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BIND_PORT=5432 LD_PRELOAD=$PWD/libuibv.so app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE
Select the packet transport independently of the wire protocol.
.br
Default: udp\-io\-uring
.br
Accepted values: udp\-io\-uring, udp\-sync, udp\-zc\-afxdp, or tcp\-devmem
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=udp\-sync ./examples/direct_traffic rocev2\fP
.TP
.B UIB_UDP_MODE
Select ordinary UDP sockets or raw RoCEv2 interoperability.
.br
Default: socket
.br
Accepted values: socket or raw; raw requires CAP_NET_RAW.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_UDP_MODE=raw LD_PRELOAD=$PWD/libuibv.so ibv_rc_pingpong\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_RX_MODE
Select multishot receive or the portable batched fallback.
.br
Default: auto
.br
Accepted values: auto, multishot, or batch
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_RX_MODE=batch ./tests/loopback\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_RX_BATCH
Set RX CQEs reaped per worker pass and batched RX depth.
.br
Default: 64
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 256
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_RX_BATCH=128 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_TX_BATCH
Limit send SQEs submitted by the io_uring worker per pass.
.br
Default: 64
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 256
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_TX_BATCH=128 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_SQPOLL
Enable the optional io_uring kernel submission polling thread.
.br
Default: off
.br
Accepted values: off or on
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_SQPOLL=on ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_SQPOLL_IDLE
Set how long an idle io_uring SQPOLL thread keeps polling.
.br
Default: 2000
.br
Accepted values: A positive number of milliseconds.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_SQPOLL=on UIB_URING_SQPOLL_IDLE=100 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_URING_SQPOLL_CPU
Pin the optional io_uring SQPOLL kernel thread to one CPU.
.br
Default: Unset.
.br
Accepted values: An online CPU number.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_URING_SQPOLL=on UIB_URING_SQPOLL_CPU=3 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_ZEROCOPY
Control optional socket and AF_XDP transmit zero\-copy.
.br
Default: auto
.br
Accepted values: off, auto, on, or required
.br
Example: \fBUIB_ZEROCOPY=required ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_ZEROCOPY_THRESHOLD
Override the minimum packet size used for socket zero\-copy.
.br
Default: 10240 in auto mode; 1024 in on or required mode.
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative byte count.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_ZEROCOPY_THRESHOLD=4096 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.SS "UDP transports"
.TP
.B UIB_UDP_GSO
Combine equal\-sized RDMA packets into UDP GSO sends. on fails context creation when the kernel does not support UDP GSO; auto falls back.
.br
Default: auto
.br
Accepted values: auto, off, or on
.br
Example: \fBUIB_UDP_GSO=off ./examples/stress_bench \-\-protocol rocev2\fP
.SS "AF_XDP transport"
.TP
.B UIB_AFXDP_IFACE
Select the netdev to which the AF_XDP socket is attached.
.br
Default: Unset; AF_XDP is unavailable until it is set.
.br
Accepted values: A local network\-interface name.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_AFXDP_IFACE=eth0 UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=udp\-zc\-afxdp app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_AFXDP_QUEUE
Select the hardware RX/TX queue used by the AF_XDP socket.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative queue identifier.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_AFXDP_QUEUE=1 UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=udp\-zc\-afxdp app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_AFXDP_PEER_MAC
Set the fixed next\-hop destination MAC for emitted frames.
.br
Default: Unset; it is mandatory for AF_XDP.
.br
Accepted values: A six\-octet colon\-separated MAC address.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_AFXDP_PEER_MAC=02:00:00:00:00:02 app\fP
.SS "TCP devmem transport"
.TP
.B UIB_DEVMEM_IFACE
Select the netdev whose RX queue receives DMA\-BUF binding.
.br
Default: Unset; device\-memory queue binding is disabled.
.br
Accepted values: A local network\-interface name.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_DEVMEM_IFACE=eth0 UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=tcp\-devmem app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_DEVMEM_QUEUE
Select the netdev RX queue used for DMA\-BUF binding.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative queue identifier.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_DEVMEM_QUEUE=1 UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=tcp\-devmem app\fP
.SS "Provider\-owned host\-memory receive"
.TP
.B UIB_HOST_ZC
Enable TCP io_uring ZCRX when its NIC queue and kernel support are usable.
.br
Default: auto
.br
Accepted values: auto, off, or required
.br
Example: \fBUIB_HOST_ZC=required UIB_HOST_ZC_IFACE=eth0 app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_HOST_ZC_IFACE
Select the interface whose hardware receive queue backs the ZCRX arena.
.br
Default: Unset; ZCRX remains inactive.
.br
Accepted values: A network\-interface name configured for TCP header/data split.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_HOST_ZC_IFACE=eth0 UIB_TRANSPORT_MODE=tcp\-devmem app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_HOST_ZC_QUEUE
Select the flow\-steered hardware queue registered with io_uring ZCRX.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative hardware receive\-queue identifier.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_HOST_ZC_QUEUE=1 UIB_HOST_ZC_IFACE=eth0 app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_VIRTME_KERNEL
Select the kernel image used by the focused host zero\-copy VM tests.
.br
Default: Unset; virtme\-ng chooses its default kernel.
.br
Accepted values: A kernel image path accepted by vng \-\-run.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_VIRTME_KERNEL=/boot/vmlinuz\-test make host\-zc\-virtme\-test\fP
.SS "Ultra Ethernet"
.TP
.B UIB_UET_CC
Select NSCC congestion control or disable it for comparison.
.br
Default: nscc
.br
Accepted values: nscc or none
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet UIB_UET_CC=none ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_UET_NSCC_MAX_WND
Cap the initial NSCC congestion window for experiments.
.br
Default: The maximum window calculated by NSCC configuration.
.br
Accepted values: A byte count no smaller than the active MTU.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet UIB_UET_NSCC_MAX_WND=65536 app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_UET_OPTIMIZED
Select the SES request\-header optimization policy.
.br
Default: auto
.br
Accepted values: off, auto, small, or medium
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet UIB_UET_OPTIMIZED=medium app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_UET_MULTIPATH
Select entropy multipathing and path\-failure tracking mode.
.br
Default: off
.br
Accepted values: off, oblivious, or path\-aware
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet UIB_UET_MULTIPATH=path\-aware app\fP
.TP
.B UIB_UET_DEBUG
Enable diagnostic UET packet and completion logging.
.br
Default: Unset and disabled.
.br
Accepted values: Any non\-empty value enables logging.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROTOCOL=uet UIB_UET_DEBUG=1 ./tests/loopback\fP
.SS "Stress benchmark executable"
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_PROTOCOL
Select the protocol when \-\-protocol is not supplied.
.br
Default: uet
.br
Accepted values: rocev2, uet, or dummy
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_PROTOCOL=rocev2 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_MEMORY
Select the memory kind used for benchmark payloads.
.br
Default: host
.br
Accepted values: host, dmabuf, or gpu\-dmabuf
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_MEMORY=dmabuf ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_ROLE
Select local or remote endpoint operation.
.br
Default: local
.br
Accepted values: local, server, or client
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_ROLE=server ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_BIND
Set the local IPv4 address in remote benchmark mode.
.br
Default: A role\-specific loopback address.
.br
Accepted values: An IPv4 address assigned to the local host.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_BIND=192.0.2.1 UIB_BENCH_ROLE=server ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_PEER
Set the remote server address used by a benchmark client.
.br
Default: Unset; it is required in client mode.
.br
Accepted values: A reachable IPv4 address.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_PEER=192.0.2.1 UIB_BENCH_ROLE=client ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_ITERATIONS
Set the number of measured RDMA operations.
.br
Default: 10000
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_ITERATIONS=100000 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_SIZE
Set the payload size of each measured operation.
.br
Default: 4096 bytes; the full matrix selects 32768.
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit byte count.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_SIZE=65536 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_WINDOW
Set the maximum number of operations kept in flight.
.br
Default: 64
.br
Accepted values: A positive queue\-window size.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_WINDOW=128 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_MTU
Set the protocol path MTU used by benchmark QPs.
.br
Default: 1500
.br
Accepted values: A positive byte count; RoCEv2 is limited to 4096.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_MTU=4096 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_CONTROL_PORT
Select the TCP control\-plane port for remote mode.
.br
Default: 19190
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 65535
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_CONTROL_PORT=20190 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_DATA_PORT
Select the UIB data\-plane port for remote mode.
.br
Default: 19100
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 65535
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_DATA_PORT=20100 ./examples/stress_bench\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_DMABUF_FD
Supply an already\-open GPU DMA\-BUF descriptor to import.
.br
Default: Unset; required by gpu\-dmabuf memory mode.
.br
Accepted values: A valid inherited file\-descriptor number.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_DMABUF_FD=9 ./examples/stress_bench \-\-memory gpu\-dmabuf\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_DMABUF_OFFSET
Set the byte offset into an imported GPU DMA\-BUF.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative byte offset.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_DMABUF_OFFSET=4096 UIB_BENCH_DMABUF_FD=9 app\fP
.SS "Complete benchmark matrix"
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_PROTOCOLS
Select the protocols traversed by the matrix runner.
.br
Default: rocev2 uet dummy
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of supported protocols.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_PROTOCOLS='rocev2 uet' make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_MEMORY_MODES
Select the memory kinds traversed by the matrix runner.
.br
Default: host dmabuf
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of host and dmabuf.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_MEMORY_MODES=host make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_AFFINITIES
Select pinned and unpinned process variants.
.br
Default: unpinned pinned
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of unpinned and pinned.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_AFFINITIES=pinned make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_MTUS
Select protocol MTUs traversed by the matrix runner.
.br
Default: 1500 4096 8192
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated list of positive byte counts.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_MTUS='1500 4096' make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_PIN_CPU
Select the pinned CPU; an explicit value pins both namespace peers to it.
.br
Default: First allowed CPU; namespace peers use first two when available.
.br
Accepted values: A CPU identifier accepted by taskset \-c.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_PIN_CPU=3 make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_OUTPUT
Select the directory receiving CSV, text, and Markdown output.
.br
Default: A timestamped directory below /tmp.
.br
Accepted values: A writable directory path.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_OUTPUT=/tmp/uib\-results make benchmark\-all\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_DOCUMENT
Select the benchmark reference document to update.
.br
Default: docs/benchmark\-results.md
.br
Accepted values: A writable Markdown file path.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_DOCUMENT=/tmp/results.md make benchmark\-doc\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_SYNC_DOCUMENT
Select the sync/async comparison document to update.
.br
Default: docs/sync\-async\-benchmark.md
.br
Accepted values: A writable Markdown file path.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_SYNC_DOCUMENT=/tmp/sync.md make benchmark\-doc\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_REUSE
Reuse CSV files in the output directory instead of rerunning.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: 0 or 1
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_REUSE=1 UIB_BENCH_OUTPUT=/tmp/run make benchmark\-doc\fP
.TP
.B UIB_BENCH_MAX_REGRESSION_PERCENT
Set the maximum aggregate UDP regression accepted by docs.
.br
Default: 5 percent
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative percentage.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_BENCH_MAX_REGRESSION_PERCENT=3 make benchmark\-doc\fP
.SS "Namespace benchmark harness"
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_KEEP_ON_FAILURE
Keep failed namespaces, interfaces, processes, and logs.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: 0 or 1
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_KEEP_ON_FAILURE=1 make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_REQUIRED
Fail instead of skipping when namespace prerequisites are absent.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: 0 or 1
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_REQUIRED=1 make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_AFFINITIES
Select pinned and unpinned namespace benchmark variants.
.br
Default: unpinned pinned
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of unpinned and pinned.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_AFFINITIES=pinned make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_MTUS
Select path MTUs for namespace benchmark endpoints.
.br
Default: 1500 4096 8192
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated list of positive byte counts.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_MTUS='1500 4096' make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_PROTOCOLS
Select protocols for the namespace benchmark matrix.
.br
Default: rocev2 uet dummy
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of supported protocols.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_PROTOCOLS=uet make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_NAMESPACE_MEMORY
Select host and DMA\-BUF namespace benchmark variants.
.br
Default: host dmabuf
.br
Accepted values: A space\-separated subset of host and dmabuf.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_NAMESPACE_MEMORY=host make namespace\-benchmark\-test\fP
.SS "Test and scaling harnesses"
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_PROTOCOL
Select the protocol used by standard ibverbs tool tests.
.br
Default: rocev2
.br
Accepted values: rocev2, uet, or dummy
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_PROTOCOL=uet make uet\-tools\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_PORT
Select the protocol service port used by standard tool tests.
.br
Default: 4791
.br
Accepted values: 1 through 65535
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_PORT=5432 UIB_TEST_PROTOCOL=uet make uib\-tools\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_ITERS
Set the operation count used by standard tool tests.
.br
Default: 64
.br
Accepted values: A positive integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_ITERS=256 make uib\-tools\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_DROP_TX
Inject one transmit loss to exercise protocol recovery.
.br
Default: Unset and disabled.
.br
Accepted values: Any non\-empty value drops one eligible packet.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_DROP_TX=1 ./tests/loopback\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_GPU_DMABUF_FD
Supply an external GPU DMA\-BUF descriptor to the import test.
.br
Default: Unset; the external GPU DMA\-BUF test skips.
.br
Accepted values: A valid inherited file\-descriptor number.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_GPU_DMABUF_FD=9 ./tests/external_dmabuf_test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_GPU_DMABUF_OFFSET
Set the starting offset in an external GPU DMA\-BUF.
.br
Default: 0
.br
Accepted values: A non\-negative byte offset.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_GPU_DMABUF_OFFSET=4096 ./tests/external_dmabuf_test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_TEST_JOBS
Set parallel jobs for optional\-feature rebuild tests.
.br
Default: 4
.br
Accepted values: A positive make job count.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_TEST_JOBS=16 make optional\-features\-test\fP
.TP
.B UIB_SCALE_THREADS
Set worker threads in the QP lookup scaling benchmark.
.br
Default: 4
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_SCALE_THREADS=8 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_SCALE_LOOKUPS
Set lookups per worker in the QP scaling benchmark.
.br
Default: 1000000
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_SCALE_LOOKUPS=5000000 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_SCALE_TRAFFIC_ITERS
Set traffic iterations for scaling protocol measurements.
.br
Default: 30000
.br
Accepted values: A positive integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_SCALE_TRAFFIC_ITERS=100000 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_MR_SCALE_LOOKUPS
Set lookups in the registered\-memory scaling benchmark.
.br
Default: 1000000
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_MR_SCALE_LOOKUPS=5000000 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_PROVIDER_CONTEXTS
Set contexts created by the provider dispatch benchmark.
.br
Default: 64
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROVIDER_CONTEXTS=128 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_PROVIDER_LOOKUPS
Set calls made by the provider dispatch benchmark.
.br
Default: 1000000
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROVIDER_LOOKUPS=5000000 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.TP
.B UIB_PROVIDER_WR_ITERS
Set calls made by the provider WR translation benchmark.
.br
Default: 100000
.br
Accepted values: A positive 32\-bit integer.
.br
Example: \fBUIB_PROVIDER_WR_ITERS=1000000 make scaling\-benchmark\fP
.SH FILES
.TP
.I libuib.so
Shared library for the direct UIB and uibv APIs.
.TP
.I libuibv.so
LD_PRELOAD provider for transparent libibverbs programs.
.TP
.I include/uib/
Installed public UIB headers.
.SH SEE ALSO
